    {
      "id": "5cba2afac392412a99c6b42d04c816e2",
      "title": "Unreal Engine Chaos",
      "description": "4.26-Chaos",
      "longDescription": "Preview 3",
      "technicalDetails": "Warning: Watch for falling rocks\n\nHelp us improve and harden the future of physics simulation in Unreal Engine with this special Chaos-enabled build. It may be a little rough around the edges, and we will be actively improving it with bug fixes and features, so we don’t recommend using it for active development. If you love being on the cutting edge of technology, or just like testing the limits of what’s possible, jump in and let us know what you think.\n\nAdditional information about this release is available on the <ExternalLink style=\"SelfUpdateError.Hyperlink\" href=\"https://forums.unrealengine.com/unreal-engine/announcements-and-releases/1843949\">Unreal Engine Forums.</>\n\nPlease submit feedback and bugs to: <ExternalLink style=\"SelfUpdateError.Hyperlink\" href=\"https://www.unrealengine.com/support/report-a-bug\">https://www.unrealengine.com/support/report-a-bug</>",
